--- §6 row 2: the SOUNDNESS control.  CFI over K4 — Aut merges the blocks, so an
    equivariant invariant MUST NOT separate them.  A split here means a bug.
  CFI(K4) [base m=4 |E|=6 |Aut(base)|=24 1-WL COARSE]   n=28   dim ker_F2(adj) = 12   Linked-classes = 28
     ✔ identity verified: Linked u v ⟺ sig u = sig v ⟺ e_u+e_v ∈ rowspace(adj)
     Linked class-size profile: {1: 28}   ⟹ the only equivariant read a relation offers (class size) is CONSTANT ⟹ VACUOUS
     soundness vs 8 edge-verified gauge automorphisms:
        (a) the RELATION `Linked` transports: ✔ 0 violations
        (b) the kernel-SIGNATURE read transports: ⛔ 144 VIOLATIONS ⟹ `sig` is NOT `ReadEquivariant` — a basis/pivot order was chosen
     cell 0 |cell|=16  ⟹ ★ SPLIT into 16 Linked-classes
     cell 1 |cell|=12  ⟹ ★ SPLIT into 12 Linked-classes
     1-WL non-singleton cells: 2   ★ split by Linked: 2   untouched: 0
     METHOD 1, refine-then-1-WL-to-fixpoint.  cells before [16, 12]
        ✔ LEGAL read (class size, equivariant): non-singleton cells 2 → 2   sizes [16, 12]
        ✔ LEGAL STEELMAN (1-WL on the 2-relation adj ∪ Linked): 2 → 2   sizes [16, 12]
        ⛔ ILLEGAL read (kernel signature, basis-dependent): 2 → 0   sizes []   — this is what a pivot order buys, and it is not available

